/-!
# Border certificates for the canonical Robinson carrier

The selected decorated substitution preserves a finite family of 376 states, each recording
a node, its coordinate parities, and selected-border observations on a three-by-three halo.
The certified observations identify the visible two-by-two cells with actual shade borders;
the halo supplies the additional cells needed for refinement.

## Main definitions

* `Canonical.BorderHalo`, `Canonical.BorderState`: local observations and their decorated node.
* `Canonical.BorderState.Admissible`: membership in the fixed finite invariant.
* `Canonical.BorderState.refine`: the local selected-border refinement.

## Main results

* `Canonical.BorderState.seed_admissible` places the outer-border seed in the invariant.
* `Canonical.BorderState.refine_admissible` proves closure under all sixteen refinements.
* `Canonical.BorderState.observations` identifies visible observations with actual shade borders.
* `Canonical.BorderState.corner_transition` classifies all index-zero child configurations.

These finite certificates support the arithmetic interpretation of the canonical carrier;
they do not assert forcing or seed removal for arbitrary tilings.

## References

The data retain `ShadedCarrierBorderHierarchyData.stateGroup0` through `stateGroup15`,
and its `refineState` rule, from
[lean-wang](https://github.com/edemaine/lean-wang/tree/64268a3), revision `64268a3`.
The mathematical background is the corrected Robinson construction in [JeandelVanier2020].
Indexed refinement witnesses compress the finite checks without changing their semantic
obligations.
-/

